# Office Presence redesign (core)

Source of truth: `docs/design/SPEC.md`, frames in `docs/design/frames/` (open the PNG with the frame name before editing a screen), and `docs/design/prototype.html`.

## Scope
- UI and information architecture only. Keep data fetching, sync, geofence, auth, and APIs working.
- Do not rename API fields, database columns, or background jobs. "Points" stays in the API; only UI text says "days".
- The only backend addition is correction requests (`docs/design/corrections-api.md`), and only when a task says so.
- One screen or one component per task.

## Brand
- Tokens only, no hex values in screens or components.
- Orange `#FD5108` only for: primary action, days bar, wordmark, selected nav. Text on orange is `#1A1A1A`.
- Green `#2ECC71` only for In and Goal met. Out is neutral grey. No red anywhere, including errors.
- No purple, indigo, teal, gradients, blur, or decorative shadow. Shadow only on sheets and drawers.
- Motion: status change (fade plus 6 px rise, 320 ms) and days bar fill (900 ms). No loops except a spinner during a request.

## Language
- "days", never "points". "8 days" target, "5 / 8 days", "3 to go", "Goal met", "Counts as 2 days".
- Buttons start with a verb. In and Out, never "checked in".
- No em dash or en dash in any UI string.
- Hours are always labeled FYI and never colored, never a bar, never a warning.

## Privacy
- Colleagues see only In or Out, since when, office name. Never GPS, coordinates, hours, or days counted.
- Admin screens never show coordinates.

## Done means
- Matches the frame in light and dark; loading, empty, and error states exist where the SPEC lists them.
- Existing tests pass, no new lint warnings, no em or en dash in strings.
